.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-agent-output 1  "output 0.3.0-beta.6"
.SH NAME
ag\-agent\-output \- Inspect saved stdout/stderr, or explicitly delete the captured text
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag agent output\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-stream\fR] [\fB\-\-delete\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIRUN\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect saved stdout/stderr, or explicitly delete the captured text
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR [\fI<NAME>\fR]
Use a server instead of this repository (without a NAME: origin)
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR \fI<STREAM>\fR
Print one stream. Text output escapes terminal controls; \-\-json preserves exact text
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
stdout
.IP \(bu 2
stderr
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-delete\fR
Permanently remove captured text, retaining the run and audit history. Remote use requires agent.operate
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIRUN\fR>
Run identifier
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0\-beta.6
